# The Flask app. Our edits live in these files — the English UI, the shared model,
# the threaded camera loop — so they have to be in the repo or a fresh clone loses
# them. The ultralytics engine (216 files) stays ignored.
!software/app/
software/app/*
!software/app/app.py
!software/app/predict_img.py
!software/app/predict_video.py
!software/app/predict_camera.py
!software/app/test_dom_ids.py
!software/app/test_export_video.py
!software/app/templates/
!software/app/static/
software/app/static/*
!software/app/static/css/
!software/app/static/js/
!software/app/static/images/
# her published result for 000013.jpg — verify_model.py says to compare against it
!software/app/static/000013_detected.jpg

# The upload folder is a working directory: whatever gets uploaded during a demo lands
# here and none of it belongs in the repo. These four are the exception — they are the
# fixtures verify_model.py and bench_enhance.py run against, and without them a fresh
# clone cannot reproduce starfish 0.83 / holothurian 0.78. URPC_test_video.mp4 stays
# out (88 MB, Drive folder), which bench_enhance.py reports and works around.
!software/app/upload/
software/app/upload/*
!software/app/upload/000013.jpg
!software/app/upload/003045.jpg
!software/app/upload/test_000080.jpg
!software/app/upload/test_000183.jpg

